  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "0029:A1",
      "kind": "A",
      "key": "1",
      "label": "The graph-lint advisory tier can accept new members, or `0006:C17` can be amended to allow it.",
      "derived": false,
      "hash": "4dbc9d6a",
      "section": "0029:§critical-assumptions",
      "line_start": 158,
      "line_end": 200,
      "bytes": 2849,
      "fields": [
        {
          "label": "Status",
          "canonical": "Status",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "Verified — ruled 2026-09-11: `0006:C17` is opened as append-only. The code already permits it; the closure was the only blocker and it is lifted.",
          "section": "0029:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0029:A1",
          "line_start": 160,
          "line_end": 162,
          "status": {
            "value": "Verified",
            "qualifier": "ruled 2026-09-11: 0006:C17 is opened as append-only. The code already permits it; the closure was the only blocker and it is lifted.",
            "tier": "canonical",
            "raw": "Verified — ruled 2026-09-11: `0006:C17` is opened as append-only. The code already permits it; the closure was the only blocker and it is lifted."
          }
        },
        {
          "label": "Method",
          "canonical": "Method",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "Peer RDR",
          "section": "0029:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0029:A1",
          "line_start": 163,
          "line_end": 163,
          "method": {
            "members": [
              "Peer RDR"
            ],
            "raw": "Peer RDR"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": "Evidence",
          "canonical": "Evidence",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "`0006:C17` states \"The advisory tier is closed at `graph-coverage-closed-by-escape`, `graph-redundant-row`, `graph-unreachable-rule`, and `graph-vacuous-atom`\" — a closure at exactly four members; 0006 is Implemented. The IMPLEMENTATION, however, imposes no such limit: severity is DERIVED, not carried per-code — `internal/graphlint/taxonomy.go::severityFor` returns `SeverityInfo` for anything `IsBlocking` rejects, and `IsBlocking` is `slices.Contains(blockingCodes, code)`. So a fifth advisory code becomes `info` with no severity plumbing, no exhaustiveness switch, and no cardinality constant anywhere in `internal/graphlint/` or `internal/cli/`; the eleven `AdvisoryCodes()` consumers all iterate. Exactly one assertion blocks it: `internal/graphlint/findings_0006_test.go::TestReq74_TheAdvisoryTierIsClosedAtExactlyFourMembers` compares `AdvisoryCodes()` to a four-element literal with `slices.Equal` — a by-value set assertion, so the fix is editing the literal, not relaxing a number.",
          "section": "0029:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0029:A1",
          "line_start": 164,
          "line_end": 179
        },
        {
          "label": "Ruling (2026-09-11)",
          "match": "author",
          "value": "C17's closure is incidental-as-then-stood, not load-bearing, and is opened. This follows `JDR 0001 §D10` rule 3, which reopened a closed `CLIError` field on a peer's request and recorded the result as \"a 0006 citation repair, not a reopening\" — the same shape. C17's load-bearing guarantee is its last sentence, \"Advisory findings MUST NOT change the success disposition,\" which adding a member does not touch; C3 restates that guarantee rather than amending it.",
          "section": "0029:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0029:A1",
          "line_start": 180,
          "line_end": 186
        },
        {
          "label": "If wrong",
          "canonical": "If wrong",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "C3 is unimplementable as written for graph-lint codes — a new finding could only enter at `blocking`, which is exactly the verdict-changing event the policy exists to prevent. Surfaces as a contradiction between this RDR and 0006 at Stage 7.1, or as an implementer unable to add an `info` code without amending a Final peer.",
          "section": "0029:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0029:A1",
          "line_start": 195,
          "line_end": 200
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0029:A2",
      "kind": "A",
      "key": "2",
      "label": "`schema_version` ships before 1.0.0, while the `0.x` series still permits incompatible change.",
      "derived": false,
      "hash": "8dba61da",
      "section": "0029:§critical-assumptions",
      "line_start": 201,
      "line_end": 221,
      "bytes": 1314,
      "fields": [
        {
          "label": "Status",
          "canonical": "Status",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "Verified",
          "section": "0029:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0029:A2",
          "line_start": 203,
          "line_end": 203,
          "status": {
            "value": "Verified",
            "tier": "canonical",
            "raw": "Verified"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": "Method",
          "canonical": "Method",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "Source Search",
          "section": "0029:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0029:A2",
          "line_start": 204,
          "line_end": 204,
          "method": {
            "members": [
              "Source Search"
            ],
            "raw": "Source Search"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": "Evidence",
          "canonical": "Evidence",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "No tag has ever been cut — `git tag --list` is empty and `git describe --tags` fails. `internal/version::resolve` defaults to `Info{Version: \"dev\", Commit: \"none\", Date: \"unknown\"}` (`internal/version/version.go::resolve`), filling commit and date from VCS stamps but never moving `version` off `\"dev\"` without an `-ldflags` injection or a module version; `internal/cli/version.go`'s verb reports that value and nothing else. `.github/workflows/release.yml` triggers only on a `v*` tag push (`on.push.tags: [\"v*\"]`). The first release is therefore 0.1.0 and the window is the whole `0.x` series rather than one release.",
          "section": "0029:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0029:A2",
          "line_start": 205,
          "line_end": 214
        },
        {
          "label": "If wrong",
          "canonical": "If wrong",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "adding `schema_version` after 1.0.0 makes the compatibility field itself a breaking change under C1's own rule, forcing a 2.0.0 for the field that exists to prevent major bumps. Surfaces as a strict-parsing consumer failing on the release that announces the compatibility promise. Note this is a *soft* deadline for the whole `0.x` series, not a hard one at 0.1.0 — the risk is procrastination past 1.0.0, not missing the first tag.",
          "section": "0029:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0029:A2",
          "line_start": 215,
          "line_end": 221
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0029:A3",
      "kind": "A",
      "key": "3",
      "label": "No current consumer parses the envelope strictly enough that one added field breaks it.",
      "derived": false,
      "hash": "708bb425",
      "section": "0029:§critical-assumptions",
      "line_start": 222,
      "line_end": 245,
      "bytes": 1497,
      "fields": [
        {
          "label": "Status",
          "canonical": "Status",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "Verified",
          "section": "0029:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0029:A3",
          "line_start": 224,
          "line_end": 224,
          "status": {
            "value": "Verified",
            "tier": "canonical",
            "raw": "Verified"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": "Method",
          "canonical": "Method",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "Source Search",
          "section": "0029:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0029:A3",
          "line_start": 225,
          "line_end": 225,
          "method": {
            "members": [
              "Source Search"
            ],
            "raw": "Source Search"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": "Evidence",
          "canonical": "Evidence",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "`DisallowUnknownFields` IS used in production, but only on the INPUT path — `internal/table/source.go::decodeStrict`, which rejects unknown keys in the model TOML under `0002:C3` (\"an unknown schema field is a stable refusal, never a silent no-op\"); its four in-repo call sites are all TOML, reached via `internal/table/load.go::Load`. There is a real in-repo consumer that re-parses the OUTPUT envelope, and it is TOLERANT: `--plan` decodes a `flow resolve --as json` envelope through `internal/cli/flow_input.go::planEnvelope`, a four-field struct read by a plain `json.Unmarshal`, which ignores unrecognized top-level properties by Go's default decoder behaviour. Test-site envelope decodes are likewise plain structs. No `.claude/` skill, hook, Makefile, or CI workflow parses the envelope at all, and `schema_version`/`format_version` appear nowhere outside this record's prose. So the additive field is safe for the strictest consumer that exists — and `planEnvelope` is the one this RDR must not break.",
          "section": "0029:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0029:A3",
          "line_start": 226,
          "line_end": 241
        },
        {
          "label": "If wrong",
          "canonical": "If wrong",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "the additive change is breaking for that consumer regardless of what C1 declares, and the rollout needs a deprecation window rather than a single release. Surfaces as a harness failing to parse immediately after upgrade.",
          "section": "0029:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0029:A3",
          "line_start": 242,
          "line_end": 245
        }
      ]
    },
    {
