        },
        {
          "label": "Evidence",
          "canonical": "Evidence",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "An enumeration of every string vocabulary reachable on the `--as=json` wire found **thirteen** emitted sets, against the seven C4 named. Every one of the five unassigned sets fits an existing tier, so no surface needs semantics the three tiers do not provide — the partition holds, which is what this assumption claims. The five, with the tier each takes (now assigned in C4): the stderr advisory `level` set `note`/`warning` (`internal/cli/respond/respond.go::Note`, `::Warn`) → `frozen`, a `type`-shaped discriminator on the second stream; the gate `verdict` set `allow`/`deny`/`indeterminate` (`internal/accessor/model.go::Verdicts`, emitted at `internal/cli/flow_exec.go::gateResult`) → `frozen`, since it is also the accessor-protocol INPUT alphabet and `cmdbind` rejects a stranger, so it cannot append without breaking gate authors; `data.escape_class` (`internal/resolve/resolve.go::RefusalKinds`, emitted at `internal/cli/flow_resolve.go`) → `frozen`, already enforced by `internal/resolve/guard_atoms_test.go::TestReq79_NoSixthRefusalKindIsMinted`; the `flow next` unknown-`reason` set (`internal/cli/flow_next.go::unknownFact.Reason`) → `append-only`, a set DISTINCT from the `graph-unprovable-coverage` `reason` set C4 already names, on a different field with a different producer; and the `graph-lint-failed` aggregate code (`internal/graphlint/taxonomy.go::AggregateCode`) → `frozen`, the one code that envelope ever carries. Two model-authored open namespaces — `findings[].class` and `data.dispositions` — are correctly tier-less: `clierr` ascribes them no meaning, so they are author surface, not CLI vocabulary. C4 also said \"the graph-lint finding codes\" where the blocking and advisory tiers take DIFFERENT tiers; it now names each.",
          "section": "0029:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0029:A4",
          "line_start": 251,
          "line_end": 277
        },
        {
          "label": "If wrong",
          "canonical": "If wrong",
          "match": "exact",
          "value": "C4 is incomplete and an unassigned surface has no stated promise — the exact gap this RDR exists to close, reappearing inside the fix. Surfaces at implementation as a vocabulary that fits no tier. This is what the enumeration above actually found, at five surfaces; the correction is C4's, not the tier vocabulary's.",
          "section": "0029:§critical-assumptions",
          "element": "0029:A4",
          "line_start": 278,
          "line_end": 282
        }
      ]
